WEBVTT

00:00:05.240 --> 00:00:06.400
Boss!

00:00:10.110 --> 00:00:11.320
Boss!

00:00:18.660 --> 00:00:24.660
<b>Dai Shogun</b>

00:00:20.200 --> 00:00:24.660
Great Revolution

00:01:45.030 --> 00:01:47.350
What happened to Kei-chan?

00:01:47.870 --> 00:01:50.460
If it continues to rampage like that...

00:01:50.900 --> 00:01:53.860
It's your fault, ice woman!

00:01:54.710 --> 00:01:55.840
Chiharu-dono!

00:01:55.840 --> 00:01:59.720
When Hyogo and I rode in it, 
we didn't have this problem!

00:01:59.720 --> 00:02:01.010
Right?

00:02:01.010 --> 00:02:05.020
If I'd been with Kei-chan in Susanoo, 
this wouldn't have happened.

00:02:07.520 --> 00:02:10.860
<b>Episode 10:
After the Rampage, 
the Two Make Their Decision</b>

00:02:10.860 --> 00:02:12.440
Listen up, you bastards!

00:02:12.440 --> 00:02:15.070
It's finally our time to shine!

00:02:16.690 --> 00:02:19.150
Kondo-san, I'm sick of waiting.

00:02:19.820 --> 00:02:22.240
The Puppets have been 
ready for a long time now.

00:02:22.240 --> 00:02:24.760
Yeah, nice work, Toshi.

00:02:24.760 --> 00:02:27.330
But is it true?

00:02:27.650 --> 00:02:31.800
Yeah, the message was brought 
to Shigeyoshi-sama personally.

00:02:31.800 --> 00:02:33.290
Thrilling, ain't it?

00:02:33.290 --> 00:02:35.310
A worthy opponent.

00:02:36.790 --> 00:02:38.340
Let's rip them apart!

00:02:39.720 --> 00:02:40.680
Where's Soji?

00:02:41.590 --> 00:02:44.130
No clue. Isn't she with you?

00:02:44.130 --> 00:02:47.020
No, I haven't seen her since morning practice.

00:02:48.290 --> 00:02:51.150
She overslept again? Jeez.

00:02:51.490 --> 00:02:54.840
Hey, Soji! We're finally going on the attack!

00:02:54.840 --> 00:02:55.860
Wake up!

00:02:57.580 --> 00:02:58.790
What?

00:03:09.440 --> 00:03:12.500
Just leave him and go, right now.

00:03:12.910 --> 00:03:15.450
That's what's best for him.

00:03:20.790 --> 00:03:22.300
Don't move.

00:03:24.230 --> 00:03:25.680
Just kidding.

00:03:26.120 --> 00:03:27.950
Scared you, didn't I?

00:03:27.950 --> 00:03:30.310
You're the rock-paper-scissors player...

00:03:30.310 --> 00:03:32.150
It's been a while.

00:03:32.150 --> 00:03:35.580
Well, have you two lovebirds been doing okay?

00:03:37.660 --> 00:03:40.080
What's wrong? There's nothing to be shy about.

00:03:43.090 --> 00:03:46.410
Don't tell me our nation's future 
leader did something stupid again.

00:03:46.410 --> 00:03:47.880
No!

00:03:49.030 --> 00:03:50.290
It's nothing.

00:03:50.290 --> 00:03:51.730
If you'll excuse me.

00:03:51.730 --> 00:03:52.890
Whoa, whoa...

00:03:52.890 --> 00:03:56.040
It must've been destiny that 
brought us here together.

00:03:56.040 --> 00:03:57.570
Come with me.

00:03:57.570 --> 00:03:59.210
Um, I can't.

00:03:59.630 --> 00:04:01.550
I-I already have...

00:04:01.920 --> 00:04:04.680
A man you care about?

00:04:06.930 --> 00:04:08.140
Not anymore...

00:04:09.720 --> 00:04:11.310
You don't have to tell me the details.

00:04:12.860 --> 00:04:16.060
Sometimes it's nice to take a little detour,

00:04:16.060 --> 00:04:18.320
Kiriko-chan.

00:04:19.280 --> 00:04:20.910
What are you—

00:04:26.810 --> 00:04:30.120
Let's go. A nice trip with a cute girl!

00:04:30.120 --> 00:04:31.790
Nonstop to America!

00:04:31.790 --> 00:04:34.120
Full speed ahead!

00:04:40.660 --> 00:04:42.050
A-America?

00:05:06.760 --> 00:05:08.930
Boss! Hang in there!

00:05:08.930 --> 00:05:10.720
So Kiriko is...

00:05:11.520 --> 00:05:13.160
I can't find her anywhere.

00:05:13.600 --> 00:05:17.520
She's probably convinced what happened 
with Keiichiro-dono was her fault.

00:05:19.350 --> 00:05:21.050
That's just great!

00:05:21.750 --> 00:05:25.340
After what she did to Kei-chan, 
she probably can't bear to face him!

00:05:25.820 --> 00:05:28.050
It's all her fault!

00:05:29.160 --> 00:05:30.930
Chiharu-san!

00:05:41.340 --> 00:05:42.650
The sea is great.

00:05:43.360 --> 00:05:45.820
You can forget all your worries.

00:05:57.530 --> 00:05:58.720
Isn't that...

00:05:58.720 --> 00:06:00.660
Yeah, a fellow pirate.

00:06:00.660 --> 00:06:03.560
You're still seasick, Maika-chan?

00:06:03.560 --> 00:06:05.520
You still haven't gotten over that?

00:06:05.520 --> 00:06:06.880
Leave me alone.

00:06:06.880 --> 00:06:08.010
You're going too fast.

00:06:08.010 --> 00:06:11.140
Go slower, more gently...

00:06:11.140 --> 00:06:13.140
Hey, I remember you!

00:06:14.920 --> 00:06:16.020
You know her?

00:06:16.020 --> 00:06:19.310
She is a villain who tried to steal Susanoo.

00:06:19.810 --> 00:06:21.650
Listen to you.

00:06:21.650 --> 00:06:24.070
I heard the rumors.

00:06:24.070 --> 00:06:27.900
That Susanoo Puppet went on a 
rampage and started wrecking things.

00:06:30.320 --> 00:06:33.390
So you're running away 'cause 
you can't stay in town anymore?

00:06:33.390 --> 00:06:35.370
You're some villain yourself.

00:06:37.960 --> 00:06:39.610
You want to fight?

00:06:39.610 --> 00:06:41.000
I'll fight you!

00:06:43.830 --> 00:06:45.300
That's the end of that.

00:06:45.300 --> 00:06:47.800
<b>She's so disgusting...</b>

00:06:49.250 --> 00:06:51.330
You seem awfully concerned about her.

00:06:52.280 --> 00:06:54.560
Are you back to your old habits, Ryoma?

00:06:54.560 --> 00:06:55.610
Yup.

00:06:55.610 --> 00:07:00.550
I love being nice to brokenhearted, vulnerable girls.

00:07:00.550 --> 00:07:01.930
Is that a problem?

00:07:02.630 --> 00:07:04.940
It's your ship. Do what you want.

00:07:04.940 --> 00:07:08.070
If you ever have your heart broken, 
Maika-chan, let me know.

00:07:08.070 --> 00:07:10.550
I'll be very nice to you.

00:07:10.550 --> 00:07:11.990
Right, Kiriko-chan?

00:07:11.990 --> 00:07:14.750
No! I haven't...

00:07:15.370 --> 00:07:17.620
Really? Sorry about that.

00:07:25.230 --> 00:07:26.510
Don't worry about her.

00:07:26.510 --> 00:07:29.480
She's got a bad attitude and a filthy 
mouth, but she's not a bad girl.

00:07:30.540 --> 00:07:33.120
No, she's right.

00:07:33.590 --> 00:07:34.550
I ran away.

00:07:38.480 --> 00:07:39.850
Ryoma-san.

00:07:40.460 --> 00:07:42.200
Remember what you once told me?

00:07:42.800 --> 00:07:45.040
That sometimes things just don't work out.

00:07:46.380 --> 00:07:52.910
I've always thought I could face 
anything for Keiichiro-sama.

00:07:53.390 --> 00:07:55.870
But I...

00:07:57.990 --> 00:07:59.350
What's this?

00:08:02.190 --> 00:08:04.050
Katsu-sensei gave this to me.

00:08:04.670 --> 00:08:06.210
A foreign sculpture?

00:08:06.210 --> 00:08:07.530
Nope.

00:08:07.530 --> 00:08:09.170
This is a globe.

00:08:09.910 --> 00:08:12.720
It shows the whole world we live on.

00:08:12.720 --> 00:08:14.040
The world?

00:08:14.040 --> 00:08:18.220
Yup. This tiny little island is where we live.

00:08:18.220 --> 00:08:20.440
And this is Nagasaki, over here.

00:08:21.030 --> 00:08:22.020
This is?

00:08:22.410 --> 00:08:24.820
Isn't it exciting?

00:08:24.820 --> 00:08:29.320
The whole world contained 
on this little round thing.

00:08:30.840 --> 00:08:32.820
Once you leave this tiny island called Japan,

00:08:32.820 --> 00:08:35.440
you can go anywhere.

00:08:35.880 --> 00:08:39.600
And all the other countries 
are connected by the sea.

00:08:40.340 --> 00:08:42.040
You can go anywhere...

00:08:42.920 --> 00:08:44.540
America is over here.

00:08:44.540 --> 00:08:49.040
The Union can get us there in a month.

00:08:49.040 --> 00:08:50.640
A month?

00:08:50.640 --> 00:08:52.340
I don't have...

00:08:52.340 --> 00:08:55.930
If you're with me, it'll be so fun, 
the time will seem to fly by.

00:08:58.710 --> 00:09:00.260
Don't worry.

00:09:00.860 --> 00:09:03.500
The world's round, like this globe.

00:09:03.500 --> 00:09:07.350
No matter where you go, you'll eventually 
end up back where you started.

00:09:09.230 --> 00:09:14.030
No matter how many detours you take, 
eventually you'll have to face yourself.

00:09:15.080 --> 00:09:17.280
That's the path a man follows.

00:09:34.080 --> 00:09:36.430
Are you Onigami?

00:09:44.680 --> 00:09:46.120
Otomi-dono.

00:09:46.120 --> 00:09:48.900
It's okay. He's just sleeping now.

00:09:48.900 --> 00:09:52.900
No, I'm worried about you.

00:09:52.900 --> 00:09:55.990
I'm fine.

00:09:55.990 --> 00:09:59.410
But I feel bad for what I've done to him.

00:09:59.780 --> 00:10:04.910
It may be that no man was ever 
meant to pilot that Onigami.

00:10:05.410 --> 00:10:08.870
So why did you let him do it?

00:10:08.870 --> 00:10:12.570
It was my mission as a ninja.

00:10:13.160 --> 00:10:14.330
Mission?

00:10:15.020 --> 00:10:22.360
Tokugawa Keiichiro is fated to go to 
Edo in Susanoo and become Shogun.

00:10:22.360 --> 00:10:25.600
That's what I raised him to do.

00:10:26.040 --> 00:10:31.440
But now, I don't know if that 
was the right thing to do.

00:10:32.000 --> 00:10:33.060
Otomi-dono.

00:10:33.640 --> 00:10:34.940
That's not true.

00:10:34.940 --> 00:10:38.620
Keiichiro-dono piloted Susanoo of his own will.

00:10:38.620 --> 00:10:40.220
You're very kind.

00:10:40.220 --> 00:10:42.820
But don't push yourself too hard.

00:10:42.820 --> 00:10:46.340
Keiichiro will be fine as long as I'm with him.

00:10:46.340 --> 00:10:50.370
You must follow your own path, 
and not be bound here.

00:10:51.170 --> 00:10:52.130
Yes, ma'am.

00:11:00.320 --> 00:11:01.800
Look at 'em all!

00:11:02.440 --> 00:11:05.370
It's a clear, starry night tonight.

00:11:16.460 --> 00:11:19.150
You don't need to say anything else.

00:11:26.520 --> 00:11:31.000
You're the first person to refuse my kiss

00:11:31.820 --> 00:11:33.580
at such perfect timing!

00:11:35.290 --> 00:11:36.480
I'm sorry.

00:11:37.410 --> 00:11:39.580
Looks like you have your answer.

00:11:44.290 --> 00:11:45.800
Ryoma-san?

00:11:51.960 --> 00:11:54.510
Follow my own path...

00:12:01.480 --> 00:12:05.520
You once asked me who I was.

00:12:06.020 --> 00:12:06.920
Yes.

00:12:06.920 --> 00:12:10.410
When I was young, I wanted to 
know the answer to that, too.

00:12:11.000 --> 00:12:13.910
Who was I, and what could I do?

00:12:14.850 --> 00:12:18.510
And then I met some people 
who'd come from beyond the sea.

00:12:18.510 --> 00:12:20.420
People from other countries?

00:12:20.760 --> 00:12:21.790
Yes.

00:12:21.790 --> 00:12:24.690
They wanted to know about me.

00:12:25.240 --> 00:12:28.720
They wanted to know what was 
happening on this island,

00:12:28.720 --> 00:12:30.430
which had been closed off for centuries.

00:12:31.360 --> 00:12:33.100
They wanted to know about us?

00:12:33.550 --> 00:12:37.520
I was aboard the Black Ships, 21 years ago.

00:12:39.520 --> 00:12:44.570
I wanted to know about other countries, 
and see how big the world is,

00:12:44.570 --> 00:12:49.580
and see how small what's happening 
on this island is compared to that.

00:12:51.080 --> 00:12:55.230
And I learned that we can't stay 
sealed away on this island forever.

00:12:56.080 --> 00:12:59.800
<b>Please open your 
country to trade</b>

00:12:56.580 --> 00:12:59.800
So I boarded the Black Ships that 
asked us to open the country to trade.

00:13:00.230 --> 00:13:06.280
But at the time, I didn't know the real 
reason they'd come to this island.

00:13:20.720 --> 00:13:22.440
It was the Onigami.

00:13:23.840 --> 00:13:26.210
I barely escaped with my life.

00:13:28.000 --> 00:13:32.830
It was terrifying, the way that thing looked.

00:13:40.010 --> 00:13:42.550
That's where this scar came from.

00:13:42.950 --> 00:13:45.480
They were after the Onigami?

00:13:45.480 --> 00:13:49.050
They call them messengers from heaven, though.

00:13:49.610 --> 00:13:50.730
From heaven?

00:13:51.280 --> 00:13:53.060
You mean messengers of the gods?

00:13:53.060 --> 00:13:57.520
Yeah. When you think about it, 
Oni are servants of the gods, too.

00:13:57.520 --> 00:13:59.730
They just serve in hell.

00:14:00.890 --> 00:14:05.740
Oni are creatures born long ago, 
when humans were first created.

00:14:06.400 --> 00:14:07.990
That's what the Onigami are?

00:14:07.990 --> 00:14:09.270
Yeah.

00:14:09.270 --> 00:14:13.120
The Tokugawa family used the 
Onigami to end the civil wars.

00:14:13.120 --> 00:14:16.920
But once the war was over, 
they were no longer needed.

00:14:17.520 --> 00:14:20.810
So the Onigami that 
survived were sealed away.

00:14:21.660 --> 00:14:24.170
And one of them was Susanoo.

00:14:24.170 --> 00:14:26.880
But the seal was broken once again.

00:14:27.530 --> 00:14:28.880
Why?

00:14:29.440 --> 00:14:30.660
Who knows?

00:14:30.660 --> 00:14:35.770
But if humans know that there's 
a great power somewhere,

00:14:36.300 --> 00:14:39.440
they can't help but use it.

00:14:39.440 --> 00:14:43.060
<b>Do you have athlete's foot?</b>

00:14:40.260 --> 00:14:42.040
How ominous.

00:14:42.650 --> 00:14:46.710
But I think there's one answer 
to be found in the fact

00:14:46.710 --> 00:14:48.950
that the foreigners think they're from heaven.

00:14:50.070 --> 00:14:53.450
That power can be used for evil...

00:14:54.500 --> 00:14:55.910
Or for good.

00:14:57.150 --> 00:15:04.090
So when the foreigners told me that an 
Onigami had revived at Edo Castle, I decided

00:15:05.030 --> 00:15:08.590
to see the man who could control 
the other Onigami for myself.

00:15:09.740 --> 00:15:11.340
Keiichiro-sama?

00:15:11.830 --> 00:15:16.390
He'll clean up this soiled country.

00:15:16.390 --> 00:15:18.730
You felt the same, didn't you?

00:15:19.100 --> 00:15:20.100
Am I wrong?

00:15:20.540 --> 00:15:26.110
Yes, I believe in Keiichiro-sama, as well.

00:15:26.110 --> 00:15:31.740
I can't swim...

00:15:27.840 --> 00:15:30.730
Looks like we'll have to go 
to America some other time.

00:15:30.730 --> 00:15:31.740
Yes.

00:15:32.760 --> 00:15:35.280
Take me back to Nagasaki, please.

00:15:35.280 --> 00:15:37.100
Well said.

00:15:37.750 --> 00:15:38.600
Look.

00:15:50.360 --> 00:15:51.840
Still sick in bed...

00:15:52.470 --> 00:15:55.470
Sorry, but I don't have time.

00:15:55.470 --> 00:15:57.430
So you're going to die here!

00:16:00.760 --> 00:16:01.690
You!

00:16:01.690 --> 00:16:04.690
I won't let you hurt Keiichiro. 
Come outside with me.

00:16:17.500 --> 00:16:20.650
Don't worry. He won't die.

00:16:20.650 --> 00:16:23.000
He's waiting for you.

00:16:23.410 --> 00:16:24.540
Ryoma-san...

00:16:25.310 --> 00:16:26.460
I...

00:16:26.460 --> 00:16:29.460
I told you. There's no need to say anything.

00:16:29.460 --> 00:16:32.130
Captain, we'll be docking soon.

00:16:33.470 --> 00:16:35.530
Weigh anchor!

00:16:40.160 --> 00:16:42.770
That's the Nagasaki dawn.

00:16:47.200 --> 00:16:49.400
It's dawn...

00:16:49.990 --> 00:16:55.030
Where did that ice woman go?

00:17:00.240 --> 00:17:01.290
Chiharu-san!

00:17:02.290 --> 00:17:03.290
Chiharu-san!

00:17:03.900 --> 00:17:06.290
Hey, Chiharu-san!

00:17:06.730 --> 00:17:08.970
Wh-What are you doing here?

00:17:08.970 --> 00:17:11.250
I thought you might be here.

00:17:11.250 --> 00:17:12.300
Why?

00:17:12.640 --> 00:17:16.050
You were looking for Kiriko-san, too, right?

00:17:16.050 --> 00:17:18.930
Are you stupid? 
I don't care about that ice woman.

00:17:19.300 --> 00:17:20.830
W-Well...

00:17:21.810 --> 00:17:23.440
Huh?

00:17:23.440 --> 00:17:24.520
What?

00:17:24.940 --> 00:17:26.420
What's that?

00:17:37.280 --> 00:17:40.030
I don't know if you're after 
us for revenge or what.

00:17:40.450 --> 00:17:43.540
But for all your talk, you're a lousy fighter.

00:17:43.540 --> 00:17:44.800
That's wrong.

00:17:44.800 --> 00:17:46.020
What is?

00:17:46.020 --> 00:17:47.960
I'm not after you for revenge.

00:17:48.710 --> 00:17:52.550
I'm fighting to protect Keiichiro.

00:17:52.550 --> 00:17:54.210
Admirable.

00:17:54.210 --> 00:17:58.200
But I'm here to kill the virgin,

00:17:58.200 --> 00:18:00.850
so whatever the case, you're in my way!

00:18:15.660 --> 00:18:16.860
Not now...

00:18:17.480 --> 00:18:18.640
What's going on?

00:18:18.640 --> 00:18:19.950
Don't worry about it!

00:18:23.360 --> 00:18:24.930
I'm out of time?

00:18:25.970 --> 00:18:28.120
Wait, are you...

00:18:32.610 --> 00:18:34.820
I'm the one who's pathetic.

00:18:35.530 --> 00:18:38.480
Kill me. You want to avenge your father, right?

00:18:38.480 --> 00:18:39.800
So kill me.

00:18:54.610 --> 00:18:55.610
I won't.

00:18:56.860 --> 00:18:59.360
I won't kill you now.

00:19:00.040 --> 00:19:01.850
Don't screw with me!

00:19:01.850 --> 00:19:05.620
Until now, I've thought of nothing but revenge.

00:19:06.060 --> 00:19:10.080
But I didn't stay here to get my revenge.

00:19:10.600 --> 00:19:14.040
I'll fight with Keiichiro, 
and go to Edo with him.

00:19:14.640 --> 00:19:16.780
That is my will.

00:19:16.780 --> 00:19:18.050
Your will?

00:19:18.720 --> 00:19:21.920
Cut the crap! You're not impressing anybody—

00:19:32.370 --> 00:19:33.310
The Shinsengumi!

00:19:33.960 --> 00:19:35.690
Soji, are you okay?

00:19:35.970 --> 00:19:37.520
Hii-chan...

00:19:37.980 --> 00:19:39.210
Kon-chan...

00:19:41.600 --> 00:19:42.580
I'm sorry.

00:19:43.200 --> 00:19:44.090
I...

00:19:45.700 --> 00:19:47.160
You didn't have to...

00:20:04.470 --> 00:20:06.150
It's them!

00:20:06.150 --> 00:20:07.720
They came sooner than we thought.

00:20:07.720 --> 00:20:08.700
Yeah.

00:20:09.450 --> 00:20:10.600
We're heading back to the ship!

00:20:25.220 --> 00:20:26.430
Keiichiro-sama!

00:20:38.060 --> 00:20:39.710
Takemikazuchi?

00:21:11.070 --> 00:21:12.300
Kiriko...

00:21:13.750 --> 00:21:15.120
Keiichiro-sama...

00:21:16.560 --> 00:21:18.420
It was you, wasn't it?

00:21:22.900 --> 00:21:27.220
Hard to starboard! Evasive maneuvers!

00:21:27.220 --> 00:21:31.180
Go fast! Go as fast as you can!

00:21:32.120 --> 00:21:34.950
It's just like it was 21 years ago.

00:21:39.280 --> 00:21:43.660
Behold the super power 
of the Armstrong Cannon!

00:21:45.920 --> 00:21:51.170
The messenger from heaven, 
the god of fury, will finally be ours...

00:23:26.170 --> 00:23:27.210
Big trouble!

00:23:27.210 --> 00:23:29.300
The Black Ships are in Nagasaki, 
and the Shogun's army, too!

00:23:29.300 --> 00:23:31.260
We can't just sit here! Let's go, Hyakusuke!

00:23:31.260 --> 00:23:33.220
It's impossible! We can't win!

00:23:33.220 --> 00:23:35.460
We have to believe in Kei-chan now!

00:23:35.460 --> 00:23:37.400
Next time, it's the eve of another 
huge battle to decide Japan's fate!

00:23:36.140 --> 00:23:39.980
<b>Next Time: 
Led by the Onigami, 
to Share Our Fate!</b>

00:23:37.400 --> 00:23:38.350
I'll show 'em!
